import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Dare to Break Free"
  description="How Dare to Break Free collects, uses and protects personal information."
>
  <article class="policy-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your information</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="policy-page__updated">Last updated: 12 November 2026</p>

    <p>This policy explains how Kali Harmen, the person behind Dare to Break Free, handles personal information when you visit daretobreakfree.co.uk or contact me through the site.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>Kali Harmen is the data controller for information you send through this website. To ask a question or exercise a privacy right, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and write “Privacy request” in your message.</p>

    <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
    <p>The contact, work-with-me and speaking forms ask for your name, email address and message or enquiry details. Depending on the form, you may also choose to provide an organisation, event details, audience information or other context. Please avoid including sensitive personal information that is not needed for your enquiry.</p>
    <p>The journaling prompt generator runs in your browser. The prompts you view or interact with are not sent to me by the generator.</p>

    <h2>How and why I use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To read and reply to a message or enquiry, and to discuss requested services or speaking engagements.</li>
      <li>To keep the correspondence needed to manage an ongoing conversation or service.</li>
      <li>To protect the forms and website from spam, misuse and technical problems.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For replies and enquiries, I rely on my legitimate interest in communicating with you. Where you are asking about a potential service, I may also use the information to take steps at your request before entering into an agreement.</p>
    <p>There is no newsletter sign-up on the website. If you ask about book updates in a message, I use your details to reply to that request, not to add you to an ongoing mailing list.</p>

    <h2>Who processes information</h2>
    <p>The website is hosted using GitHub Pages. The hosting service may process technical request information, such as your IP address and browser details, to deliver and secure the site. The forms are sent to Formspree, which processes submissions and forwards them so I can respond. Formspree says its service may process information in the United States and other countries where it operates. The site also requests fonts from Google Fonts; when your browser loads those fonts, Google receives the technical information needed to provide them.</p>
    <p>Formspree keeps a submission record in its service as well as forwarding it by email. I do not sell your personal information or use this site to run advertising profiles.</p>

    <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
    <p>I check the Formspree submissions and Gmail copies every two weeks and delete enquiries I no longer need. If an enquiry is ongoing or leads to work, I may keep the relevant correspondence for as long as needed to manage it or deal with related legal matters. Deleting a message in Gmail moves it to Trash, where Google may retain it for up to 30 days unless I permanently delete it sooner. Formspree handles any provider-side technical logs and retention under its own practices. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree’s privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/7401?hl=en-GB">Gmail’s deletion information</a>.</p>

    <h2>International processing</h2>
    <p>Some service providers may process information outside the UK. Where international transfers take place, the relevant provider is responsible for the transfer safeguards applicable to its service. See the providers’ own notices for details.</p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on the circumstances, UK data protection law gives you rights to request access to, correction or deletion of your information, to restrict or object to some processing, and to receive certain information in a portable form. To make a request, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. You can also complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p>

    <h2>Links and updates</h2>
    <p>This site may link to other websites. Their privacy practices are their own. I may update this policy when the site or its services change; the date above shows when it was last reviewed.</p>

    <h2>Provider information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree privacy policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
